{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy","id":797132,"title":"Is it time to divorce Tier from Cell/Compact/Conspiracy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T18:57:29-08:00","id":797132,"title":"Is it time to divorce Tier from Cell/Compact/Conspiracy?","content":"With Open Development in full swing, I figure it's time to bring back a debate almost as old as Hunter (and long-championed by The King's Raven): can and should Hunter organizations be viewed separately from Tiers?<br /> <br /> In every other Chronicles game, Tier is a reflection of scale and scope for your chronicle, roughly analagous to a Local/National/Global divide. Hunter is shackled to an older form of it, and one that doesn't make too much sense when viewed rationally; Tier 1 is lone individuals, Tier 2 is a membership in a group, Tier 3 is membership in a special group. This system already falls apart when looked at too hard - I'm dead certain that Network Zero has more members than the Lucifuge - but it's also the only game with this weird structure.<br /> <br /> Is an independent cell of dogged investigators travelling the globe in order to stop a vampire conspiracy not a Tier 3 game? Is a lone VALKYRIE cell, cut off from their superiors and sent to investigate why a tiny town has such a high missing persons rate not a Tier 1 game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T19:02:57-08:00","id":797134,"title":"","content":"I already do this in my games, along with decoupling Endowments from the groups they're from. I completely ignore Tiers, I allow players to pick up any Endowments they like if they can justify it with fluff (for example, a devoutly religious Hunter being &quot;blessed&quot; with Benedictions despite never having even heard of the Malleus, or a mad doctor learning to vivisect monsters and create the equivalent of Cheiron's grafts for himself and his fellow Hunters), and I ignore how big or small compacts and conspiracies are supposed to be. I tend to upscale Compacts a bit and globalise them, and then downscale the reach and power of Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> And I'll most likely keep doing this in Hunter 2.0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T19:04:40-08:00","id":797137,"title":"","content":"I'm all for divorcing Hunter organizations from Tier. Tier is useful for discussing the scope of a chronicle, but one could easily play a Tier 1 TFV game or a Tier 3 game with an unaffiliated Cell. I have a feeling that the globalizing of Compacts is a conscious step towards this, since Tier 3 is supposed to be the global Tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T19:55:00-08:00","id":797152,"title":"","content":"I'm all for the division of tiers from compacts and conspiracies, but I'm also for a redefinition of compacts and conspiracies. The Tiers have long since been tied to 'scale', and I think it's both baked into enough of the Chronicles of Darkness and useful enough to keep the idea of local, regional, and global organizations.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies and compacts, in the mean time, need to be the difference between those that employ extra-normal/supernatural means and those that don't. Network Zero is a Tier 3 compact, Promethean Brotherhood is probably a Tier 2 Conspiracy, as examples.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Both sides need to be manipulated by the supernatural as much as they are not, too. Let's have more of this careful dance between humanity and monstrosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-30-2015, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T20:11:33-08:00","id":797160,"title":"","content":"I think the Tiers definitely need to be divorced from Compacts and Conspiracies. In the 1700s travel may have been difficult and truly global organizations limited, but it's almost 2016! Anyone with some money (which every Compact likely has) can hop on an airplane for globe trotting adventures; anyone with a few bucks a month can set up a website dedicated to their cause and reach out globally.<br /> <br /> I think the difference between Compacts and Conspiracies should be the existence of centralized authority with clear chains of command: a Conspiracy has a single, powerful authority directing it (such as the US government, the Vatican, or Cheiron corporate HQ) whereas a Compact should be more diffuse and informal with many local leaders and more variance in local policies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T00:51:32-08:00","id":797223,"title":"","content":"It still kind of bugs me that the word Tier was introduced into Hunter and ment the size of the group, and was then used for something completely later; but you can't change the past.<br /> <br /> My thought's is that there's multiple important factors that all tended to get compressed into one word &quot;Tier&quot; in Hunter 1E and in 2E they should be split apart:<ul><li>The overall size/resources/power of the organisation</li> <li>Do they have an Endowment. Later expanded with the lower power Compact Endowments.</li> <li>How are they structured? The Union is bottom up. Task Force: VALKARIE are top down.</li> <li>The scope of the game.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In 2E what I'd like to see is:<ul><li>The word Tier means the scope of the game - that's fixed now.</li> <li>Compact refers to groups with a shared philosophy. Conspiracy refers to groups with an actual chain of command. This means that, for example, The Lucifuge would be a Compact (most Lucifuge are pretty independent as I understand it) and The Loyalists of Thule would be a small and underpowered Conspiracy.</li> <li>Endowment is completely divorced from other concerns. The Lucifuge would keep Castigation, the Loyalists of Thule wouldn't get a new Endowment.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Basically. When I play a Compact I want to know that me and the other PCs will be a mostly independent Cell; but we'd be expected to have certain values and ideals and there are people who have similar values and ideals we can mostly trust. If we're Null Mysteriis we'd be expected to be perusing scientific understanding, as so long as our goal remains science rather than the extermination of vampires there are people who'll have our back. If we're Task Force: VALKARIE we'd expect someone to give us orders, and perhaps the opportunity to give our subordinates orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797152#post797152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conspiracies and compacts, in the mean time, need to be the difference between those that employ extra-normal/supernatural means and those that don't. Network Zero is a Tier 3 compact, Promethean Brotherhood is probably a Tier 2 Conspiracy, as examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. It's a big thematic difference, but IMO it's a smaller thematic difference than how the organisation is structured. United We Stand and all that. I'm not sure it's nessacary to have a special keyword, but if it is I'd be partial to sticking &quot;Empowered&quot; on there. So the Promethian Brotherhood are an Empowered Compact, VASCU are an Empowered Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> I think though, I would prefer not to use a special keyword for this. Just because of the edge cases. Are Task Force: VALKARIE an Empowered group because of Advanced Armory, or are they not because AA is mostly non-supernatural? I think it might be better to just let players and Storytellers read the Endowment section (and status benefits) and apply their own judgement on what that Endowment means for the themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also like to draw a distinction between groups who're strictly anti-supernatural. Groups who've got a few non-reproducable tricks, and groups with the ability to grant all their membership some mojo - with only the last of these being an Endowment.<br /> <br /> E.G. The Long Night might have one or two members who can call down miracles from God, but they can't teach anyone or only 1 in 100 students learns enough to pull of a working miracle. The Malleus Maleficarum can teach just about anyone to use Benedictions; so that's an Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-31-2015, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T03:26:19-08:00","id":797258,"title":"","content":"I'm beginning to wonder if we really need the difference between Compact and Conspiracy. I mean, really, what's the difference between them? It used to be scope - but now that's dying away. It used to be a shiny merit, but that blurs when we look at the options in Compacts and Conspiracy book. <br /> <br /> Do we really need an entire new classification for some organizations with Endowments? Especially when Endowments can come or go depending on the individual game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T05:53:42-08:00","id":797297,"title":"","content":"I concur with MCN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:35:10-08:00","id":797312,"title":"","content":"I'm also all in for separating Tier of play from Compacts and Conspiracies. To use most <b>Hunter </b>appropriate media inspirations - <b>The X Files </b>are chronicle about VASCU cell on Tier 1, without all backing up or Teleinformatics powers. In meanwhile <b>Supernatural</b> is non-organisation play from Tier 1 to Tier 3 and back again, in that Winchesters save single people, then rescue a one state and then save whole world - all without rally joining any Compact or Conspiracy. ( Well, there was Roadhouse in season 2, but it was still more &quot;we are only meeting some hunters from it - we are not part of that crew&quot; kinda thing. )<br /> <br /> I say that we should separate Tier of play from structure of organisation. All Compact and Conspiracies can be split in to those groups ( from the bottom ) that have geographical jurisdictions:<br /> 1. Cell - Town, city's district.<br /> 2. Chapter House ( Division?) - Region, small country, state in Americas.<br /> 3. Headquarters (HQ) - Whole globe.<br /> <br /> And with this partition we easily can have Compacts that are based on Chapter Houses from whole the world. each slightly different and with local variation, maybe even it's own name - but still answering as one Compacts name. We can have one &quot;Union&quot;, that is divide in to lesser Chapter Houses ( various &quot;unions&quot;), each with it's own agenda in the bigger creed of Compact, leaders and even names. Our Chapter Houses may even fight between themselves. Or that we can various &quot;congregation&quot; of Long Night, each being different church in reality. Compacts still can have one HQ, but it's center of the group only in name - each Chapter House is in reality independent. Each &quot;Ashwood Abbey&quot; Chapter House is, in reality, different Hellfire Club, with it's own name, policies, leaders. First Chapter is more the model to repeat or embody than direct commander.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies, then, are groups with direct chain of command. HQ is sending orders, you must to obey them. Chapter Houses can still fight, but central make sure it's not all out conflict and in the end - you are agent to the same force, nor similar.<br /> <br /> It's nicely sum up mine idea - Chapter Houses in Compact are<i> loosely similar ( </i>and could be name differently ), Chapters in Conspiracy are the <i>same</i>, in the end.<br /> <br /> And yes, in this model, Loyalists of Thule becomes Conspiracy, because of the power Three Man of Munich on the rest of members. Probably Ascending Ones, as so loose, various cults, become then Compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-01-2016, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T06:47:01-08:00","id":797323,"title":"","content":"I don't really use the Compact/Conspiracy definitions in my play, so I wouldn't mind being rid of them. Especially because the word &quot;Conspiracy&quot; is a bit loaded, and people might have preconceptions that the text later proves wrong. I wouldn't mind having all Hunter organisations referred to as &quot;Compacts&quot; and then giving them all Endowments, some of which are overtly supernatural (such as Castigations or Benedictions) and others are not (such as the Compact Endowments from Compacts and Conspiracies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T11:18:07-08:00","id":797432,"title":"","content":"I'm going to echo what others said - they need to be separate. Whether the Compact/Conspiracy division is even needed is a fair question to ask, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:02:58-08:00","id":797476,"title":"","content":"I think that at the least, there needs to be a more mechanical distinction between Conspiracies and Compacts, and that there should be a distinction. Global scale and access to travel is independent of this distinction, the real question I feel is that of <i>power </i>and <i>obligation</i>. I don't mind compacts getting Endowments, but I do think when you're in a Conspiracy, there should be some mechanical presence representing the privileges you get from being in a well connected and hopefully well funded organization that at the least, has some sort of infrastructure for you to call upon for information or narrative control. That's the power part, that the Conspiracy (and by extension, you) is deep in this shit. They don't just investigate secrets, <i>they also create them</i>. Those secrets give them power, but are also a big weakness. Compromising those secrets is not in the conspiracy's interests.<br /> <br /> Now, compacts have secrets as well, but I think the difference is that compacts remain loose enough to where they can survive where conspiracies can't, that any secrets they have effect individuals more than they do the organization as a whole. Mechanically you could represent this as Hunters in a conspiracy having standing or assigned orders they must obey or get shafted, something like that. As long as there's some meat to the idea that being in a conspiracy means being <i>obligated </i>to uphold their secrets and expectations. <br /> <br /> I will agree that geographic scope should be independent of this distinction. The lone VALKYRIE cell in the OPs example I think is still a tier 3 game because the PCs in that scenario should have more resources and tools (they are still government agents with Advanced Armory gadgets and training from peers who have dealt with the occult) to call upon to figure out why there's so many missing people, and more importantly have more ability to deal with a cause that's far weirder and more dangerous than what a less connected cell that's either working independently or in a compact can be expected to handle. It doesn't matter what the cause actually is, they just have more options.<br /> <br /> So...no, I don't think tiers need to be divorced from compacts and conspiracies, but we do need to reaffirm what they mean, and emphasize those differences mechanically to give players and storytellers some neat new tools to play with to represent the pros and cons from joining such organizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:22:51-08:00","id":797490,"title":"","content":"seeing how Tier and Endowment access would be revised is one of the things I look forward the most in the new edition. The new blog post has showed us a bit of how Monica thinks about Compacts in the Slasher Chronicles, and it seems they would take a lot bigger place in the setting. Until now, I think I like how things are going, so I think I'll put some trust in her and wait to see how she thinks about the place of Conspiracies in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:25:09-08:00","id":797491,"title":"","content":"It's also perfectly possible to relegate the word Conspiracy to Deviant and keep all Hunter organizations as Compacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T21:59:37-08:00","id":797657,"title":"","content":"Chalk me up for another vote in favor of divorcing Tier and style of organization. Being free to mix and match seems like it will help so many groups that were shoved into one or the other because they needed an Endowment or what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T02:40:18-08:00","id":797730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797297#post797297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I concur with MCN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me as well, the distinction was rather arbitrary and born out of tier system, if the organisations are no longer clarified by tier (and thusly by having an endowment), the distinction looses all meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10044-arcanephysics","name":"ArcanePhysics","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T02:49:43-08:00","id":797732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797134#post797134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already do this in my games, along with decoupling Endowments from the groups they're from. I completely ignore Tiers, I allow players to pick up any Endowments they like if they can justify it with fluff (for example, a devoutly religious Hunter being &quot;blessed&quot; with Benedictions despite never having even heard of the Malleus, or a mad doctor learning to vivisect monsters and create the equivalent of Cheiron's grafts for himself and his fellow Hunters), and I ignore how big or small compacts and conspiracies are supposed to be. I tend to upscale Compacts a bit and globalise them, and then downscale the reach and power of Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> And I'll most likely keep doing this in Hunter 2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is off topic, but since it's in the thread, I'd like to say that this is how I would like to see endowments in the Slasher Chronicle, where you get a menu of endowments, and organisations have write-ups on which are most thematically appropriate and how to flavour them. So Lucifuge could get Relic equivalent, and Chieron get some Advanced Armoury, Long Night could get something similar to Benedictions etc. More in line with how powers work for other splats. The power sets of endowments would likely have to grow more generic, while the flavour would come from organisation the hunter belongs to...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10044-arcanephysics","name":"ArcanePhysics","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T04:43:07-08:00","id":797746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcanePhysics</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797732#post797732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power sets of endowments would likely have to grow more generic</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I'm against this idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T05:06:26-08:00","id":797752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcanePhysics</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797732#post797732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is off topic, but since it's in the thread, I'd like to say that this is how I would like to see endowments in the Slasher Chronicle, where you get a menu of endowments, and organisations have write-ups on which are most thematically appropriate and how to flavour them. So Lucifuge could get Relic equivalent, and Chieron get some Advanced Armoury, Long Night could get something similar to Benedictions etc. More in line with how powers work for other splats. The power sets of endowments would likely have to grow more generic, while the flavour would come from organisation the hunter belongs to...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, personally I wouldn't do that. I would simply give flavour to the power itself, and then let the player come up with a character concept where that Endowment fits. That way, you don't get generic powers, because each individual power is rich with fluff, but you also don't restrict it to an organisation.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you don't really need to do anything different from what Hunter already does. You can say that the Malleus teaches Benedictions and has adopted that as its signature Endowment, but that plenty of non-affiliated faithful develop Benedictions on their own, and that the Malleus often recruits them because they see them as blessed (or hunts them down because they're heretics, however the devs want to spin it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T06:06:58-08:00","id":797767,"title":"","content":"personally, I always see Endowments not as what a conspiracy's Hunter can do, but as what the Hunter's conspiracy can provide- that is, a singular hunter may get a single power equivalent to a specific Endowment or even develop it all alone- but the ability to widespread teach Endowments to many members in a relatively safe and reliable way should be something that only a Conspiracy should do. It means something about the role of Endowments in the setting, for unlike other games where the Kewel Powerz define the character, Endowments define the character's organization, status and connection to other hunters. It reinforce the theme of teamwork and &quot;together we stand&quot;, showing that hunters may be weak alone in the dark, but together they can accomplish new feats which are not available to the singular hunter. Plus, Endowments represent the Conspiracy's history, resources and collective knowledge which shape its identity. It is not just a &quot;supernatural merit&quot;, but something which ties all the members together and show them they are a part of something bigger. When you shoot a monster with a Mjolnir Cannon, you don't just use a cool piece of tech- you blast the bastard with the might of the United States of America!*<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I view the role of Endowments in the setting- not as supernatural powers, but as the power of the collective, the highest humanity can reach as a group. This is why I don't think Endowment Access or definition of Compact verse Conspiracy should be divorced in general from Tiers, especially when you look at the organization's Tier less as the &quot;number of members&quot; and more as the &quot;reach and level of influence an organization has&quot;. It is not about having hunters who identify themselves as members all across the world- it is about being able to activate members all across the world. The Lucifuge may be small, but the Lady's grip over all 666 members is powerful enough to let her deploy them all over Europe, the US and beyond- something Network Zero may find a lot harder to accomplish.<br /> <br /> In sort, I'm eagerly waiting for the future Conspiracy/Endowments blog posts to see how Monica would place them in the setting.<br /> <br /> *yeah, I know that the Lucifuge and the Otodo's Endowments seem to be an exception, but both are exceptions in general- and maybe some thing about them would change in the new edition. Still, I'll argue that while the potential for Castigations is found for every Child of 7th Generation, only the members of the Lucifuge know how to shape them into specific rites which were developed by the Lady (I think it was hinted to be the case in the core book. I'm not sure, need to check it). The same goes for the Otodo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:05:05-08:00","id":797787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797746#post797746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why I'm against this idea.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A valid point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10044-arcanephysics","name":"ArcanePhysics","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:06:18-08:00","id":797790,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everything Lost Light said.<br /> <br /> Except that I would allow a Compact to have an Endowment, with a note that such a Compact is either going to use it's Endowmnet to grow or quite likely have someone come along and steal it if it does't get big enough to defend itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:11:09-08:00","id":797793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797790#post797790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much everything Lost Light said.<br /> <br /> Except that I would allow a Compact to have an Endowment, with a note that such a Compact is either going to use it's Endowmnet to grow or quite likely have someone come along and steal it if it does't get big enough to defend itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll support that option, simply because it opens up an option for making great stories :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:21:19-08:00","id":797799,"title":"","content":"I think that A) there is nothing wrong with Endowments as &quot;cool merits&quot;, it's just as valid a playstyle as any other; and B) there's a wide gulf between &quot;Endowments as cool merits&quot; and &quot;Endowments can exist and manifest without a Conspiracy behind them.&quot; If one advocates for the maximum variety of stories, then clearly having it both ways (Endowments as both spontaneously manifesting and taught/shared by a Conspiracy) provide the widest possible coverage.<br /> <br /> I also have no idea how an Endowment can be stolen. Even if they are literally physical objects like Relics, Elixirs and Advanced Armoury, you can have either recipes/schematics (for Elixirs and Advanced Armoury) or you can physically protect them like the Aegis Kai Doru is repeatedly stated to do. Or, you know, since your Compact is all about hunting down relics and you are the expert on that field, you could also, you know, recover them. Or get more.<br /> <br /> There's really no circumstance where an Endowment can be stolen. Replicated? Absolutely. But outright stolen with no way of protecting it, recovering it or getting more? Don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:50:11-08:00","id":797809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797799#post797799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that A) there is nothing wrong with Endowments as &quot;cool merits&quot;, it's just as valid a playstyle as any other; and B) there's a wide gulf between &quot;Endowments as cool merits&quot; and &quot;Endowments can exist and manifest without a Conspiracy behind them.&quot; If one advocates for the maximum variety of stories, then clearly having it both ways (Endowments as both spontaneously manifesting and taught/shared by a Conspiracy) provide the widest possible coverage.<br /> <br /> I also have no idea how an Endowment can be stolen. Even if they are literally physical objects like Relics, Elixirs and Advanced Armoury, you can have either recipes/schematics (for Elixirs and Advanced Armoury) or you can physically protect them like the Aegis Kai Doru is repeatedly stated to do. Or, you know, since your Compact is all about hunting down relics and you are the expert on that field, you could also, you know, recover them. Or get more.<br /> <br /> There's really no circumstance where an Endowment can be stolen. Replicated? Absolutely. But outright stolen with no way of protecting it, recovering it or getting more? Don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the &quot;problem&quot; (if you call it as such, for seeing it as a problem or not is depends on individual storyteller) is that mechanics are meant in order to tell the story better. The way that Endowments are build right now makes you to tell a certain story- a story about teamwork, ideology and shared history. You can't just have the merit, you need to join a Conspiracy to do so, which means you must (at least partially) agree with the group's agenda and point of view on the world. You can't call down Benedictions without joining the Catholic Church, you can't evoke the Goetic Gospels without agreeing the magic should not be destroyed. Making Endowments into something any hunter (or actually, any mortal) could learn freely under the right conditions would harm that story- which could work is you want to play a Supernatural style monster hunter which could use all kinds of cool tricks without real commitment to a bigger organization. While I'm not saying it is not a valid way to play Hunter, I don't think that this is the story the game tries to tell- a setting hack, maybe, but not the default case.<br /> <br /> And about stealing Endowments- Conspiracies are monopolies. The powers they perfected through the years are done because they invested time, resources and manpower at discovering and shaping them. Stealing Endowments from a Conspiracy or a rising Compact means stealing their secrets and technique, something which could be done especially when the conspiracy is young and weak. Let's look at the Promethean Brotherhood as an example- for now, they are working on translating the Rite of Hecate and perfecting it. If you steal the ritual and destroy their records, you would greatly harm their ability to use it. While some may have memorized parts of it or have their own copies, if the group is small enough and you are big enough, you could target all of the &quot;big names&quot; in the group and either kill them or simply destroy their libraries. You may even kidnap a few and force what they know about the ritual out of them. You don't even need to kill all the members of the compact- just the important ones. Those who are left beyond may try to reestablish themselves, yet without references to the original rite and with their leaders down, there is little they can do- after all, there is a good chance the ritual would kill them if they'll use it wrongly, and they eventually give up. You, on the other hand, has the secrets of a new Endowment in your hands, which you could use either use for your own advantage or destroy. Doing so to a full grown conspiracy would be a lot harder to do, but in the case of a full scale war it may be done.<br /> <br /> In sort, when you steal an Endowment, you steal a part of the Conspiracy's own foundations, and you do it by destroying it and make sure it would not rise again- especially if that someone tries to copy your precious resource you worked years to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T07:51:20-08:00","id":797810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797799#post797799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have no idea how an Endowment can be stolen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for Advanced Armory, steal the blue prints, the origonal research, then burn all the originals. For Benediction, steal all the books that teach the Endowment.<br /> <br /> Tough to do against a major operation like TF:V, but against a smaller Compact then sure.<br /> <br /> That's assuming that the Endowment doesn't have a single point of failure. You could have an Endowment where everyone gets powers by touching a special Relic - steal that Relic and it's yours.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninjaed by Lost Light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:13:48-08:00","id":797822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797809#post797809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the &quot;problem&quot; (if you call it as such, for seeing it as a problem or not is depends on individual storyteller) is that mechanics are meant in order to tell the story better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone agrees with that assumption. People see mechanics and their purpose in different ways. For some, it's a way to arbiter conflict (mostly between NPCs and PCs). For others, they allow the players to exert narrative control over the story in tangible ways that they can tinker with but still have an element of chance (this is what sets mechanics-heavy systems apart from rules-light or freeform RPGs: the uncertain outcome that can be steered in one direction but never fully controlled). And yet for others, mechanics are fun in and of themselves, because they're empowering, or something to fiddle with, or something that is their own in a tangible way.<br /> <br /> And even if we go by your assumption that mechanics must always be subordinated to a story, you're still assuming that there is only One True Story to be told: either you're a completely average human with no Endowments, or you're an Endowed Hunter that must belong to a Conspiracy, and must (as you described) agree with the Conspiracy's ideologies to a certain degree.<br /> <br /> I don't think those are the only stories you can tell with Hunter: The Vigil, nor do I necessarily think the book implies those are the &quot;main&quot; stories either. I think that a Catholic priest who never heard of the Malleus is a good candidate for spontaneously developing Benedictions, just like a paranoid gunsmith could develop Advanced Armoury, an occult-minded chemist could brew Elixirs, an antiquarian might unearth Relics, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797810#post797810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for Advanced Armory, steal the blue prints, the origonal research, then burn all the originals. For Benediction, steal all the books that teach the Endowment.<br /> <br /> Tough to do against a major operation like TF:V, but against a smaller Compact then sure.<br /> <br /> That's assuming that the Endowment doesn't have a single point of failure. You could have an Endowment where everyone gets powers by touching a special Relic - steal that Relic and it's yours.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninjaed by Lost Light.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually further support for the idea that Endowments can develop spontaneously outside Conspiracies. If Endowments were that vulnerable, they would've been stolen/destroyed already, particularly by powerful supernatural creatures, or simply creatures that the Conspiracy doesn't normally target or is ill-prepared to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:46:01-08:00","id":797831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797822#post797822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not everyone agrees with that assumption. People see mechanics and their purpose in different ways. For some, it's a way to arbiter conflict (mostly between NPCs and PCs). For others, they allow the players to exert narrative control over the story in tangible ways that they can tinker with but still have an element of chance (this is what sets mechanics-heavy systems apart from rules-light or freeform RPGs: the uncertain outcome that can be steered in one direction but never fully controlled). And yet for others, mechanics are fun in and of themselves, because they're empowering, or something to fiddle with, or something that is their own in a tangible way.<br /> <br /> And even if we go by your assumption that mechanics must always be subordinated to a story, you're still assuming that there is only One True Story to be told: either you're a completely average human with no Endowments, or you're an Endowed Hunter that must belong to a Conspiracy, and must (as you described) agree with the Conspiracy's ideologies to a certain degree.<br /> <br /> I don't think those are the only stories you can tell with Hunter: The Vigil, nor do I necessarily think the book implies those are the &quot;main&quot; stories either. I think that a Catholic priest who never heard of the Malleus is a good candidate for spontaneously developing Benedictions, just like a paranoid gunsmith could develop Advanced Armoury, an occult-minded chemist could brew Elixirs, an antiquarian might unearth Relics, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that there is only &quot;one true story&quot;. I'm saying that when a Developer deigns a game, he needs to decide which game is it going to be, and the mechanics he creates evolve around the themes he wish to put in the front. As a player or a ST, you can do whatever you want with the mechanics- which is why there are setting hacks and homebrews, but a Developer needs to make mechanics while thinking how they are both fun AND serve the game's themes. Just like in the regular D&amp;D game a fighter can't cast spells and a cleric doesn't have a warlock pact with demons because the division into classes is an important aspect for the game, if the Developer decides that binding each Endowment to a Conspiracy serves the themes of the game better than letting everyone learns Endowments freely, then it is the Developer's right to do so- which is funny, considering we still have no clue how Monica thinks about the subject. No one is saying that you are playing your game wrong- only that it is not what the Developer had in mind.<br /> <br /> Also, notice I didn't said anything about stopping individuals from spontaneously developing single Endowments, or even a number of them- only that they can't share them freely with other members, either because that don't know how (like the Inspired Priest) or lack resources (like the paranoid gunsmith), and if a certain Conspiracy would find out about them they are going either to recruit them or attack them, depends if they seem them as an assess or as a threat to their monopoly. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is actually further support for the idea that Endowments can develop spontaneously outside Conspiracies. If Endowments were that vulnerable, they would've been stolen/destroyed already, particularly by powerful supernatural creatures, or simply creatures that the Conspiracy doesn't normally target or is ill-prepared to deal with. </div> </div> </div>first, Major Templates can't use most Supernatural Merits, so they can't use most of the Endowments. Second, the conspiracies that still exist are the ones which survived- many have fallen through history, and many would fall in the future. Such organization are weak when they are young and don't have a strong leadership- but once they grow enough, destroying them or stealing their secrets would be a lot harder to accomplish. There is a major difference between destroying something like the Barret Commission and destroying Task Force VALKYRIE- and it is not because of the Endowments. It is because of the size. of the group in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:47:19-08:00","id":797833,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you can say tearing up the entire of VALKYRIE and destroying their accumulated knowledge is &quot;vulnerable&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:08:10-08:00","id":797842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797831#post797831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just like in the regular D&amp;D game a fighter can't cast spells and a cleric doesn't have a warlock pact with demons because the division into classes is an important aspect for the game,</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet some of the most popular aspects of D&amp;D are multiclassing, hybrid classing, Prestige Classing, feats that give you access to things that belong to other classes and so on. People like customising and fiddling with mechanics, often in order to mechanically represent specific concepts that the Developer's original vision did not cover (such as a fighter that casts spells or a cleric that makes pacts with demons).<br /> <br /> I consider myself a staunch supporter of flexibility, options and a &quot;restaurant menu&quot; approach to mechanics and fluff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797831#post797831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, notice I didn't said anything about stopping individuals from spontaneously developing single Endowments, or even a number of them- only that they can't share them freely with other members, either because that don't know how (like the Inspired Priest) or lack resources (like the paranoid gunsmith), and if a certain Conspiracy would find out about them they are going either to recruit them or attack them, depends if they seem them as an assess or as a threat to their monopoly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be a good compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:24:46-08:00","id":797848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797842#post797842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet some of the most popular aspects of D&amp;D are multiclassing, hybrid classing, Prestige Classing, feats that give you access to things that belong to other classes and so on. People like customising and fiddling with mechanics, often in order to mechanically represent specific concepts that the Developer's original vision did not cover (such as a fighter that casts spells or a cleric that makes pacts with demons).<br /> <br /> I consider myself a staunch supporter of flexibility, options and a &quot;restaurant menu&quot; approach to mechanics and fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, in my games multiclassing was rarely used, and even when it was it was for just a level or two, nothing more or a Prestige Class (which is built around your base class in many ways). That only shows you that things like &quot;menu&quot; version of a game are something which depends on a certain group, which means it is a supplements material, not a Core thing. The same goes for Hunter- the game needs certain themes to build upon, and future supplements may expand those mechanics or offer variations, but the Core assumption should be that Endowments should come from Conspiracies, IMO.<br /> <br /> and with those words, I'm going to start focus on my homeworks or else I'll never finish them in time :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:33:46-08:00","id":797851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=797848#post797848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, in my games multiclassing was rarely used, and even when it was it was for just a level or two, nothing more or a Prestige Class (which is built around your base class in many ways). That only shows you that things like &quot;menu&quot; version of a game are something which depends on a certain group, which means it is a supplements material, not a Core thing. The same goes for Hunter- the game needs certain themes to build upon, and future supplements may expand those mechanics or offer variations, but the Core assumption should be that Endowments should come from Conspiracies, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're going to use anecdotal experience to justify what is Core and what is Supplement, I'm going to say that in my 15+ years of playing RPGs, I've never seen a single player <i>not</i> multiclass or PrC, at least for a level or two. And by building up on that, I would structure the 2e corebook with groups on one chapter and Endowments on another, and simply have a line at the end of each group as to the Endowment they offer (perhaps at an XP discount? Or buyable with PXP?), and then have a clear introductory paragraph in the Endowment chapter that details how any Hunter can pick up any Endowment if they can justify it.<br /> <br /> See, I can use the same reasoning too. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:28:48-08:00","id":798309,"title":"","content":"I would say there's two kinds of Tier sets in HtV: there's Tiered PC groups, and there's Tiers for chronicle scope. To use Supernatural as an example, that's pretty firmly a Tier 1 cell playing in a Tier 2 game that reaches Tier 3 by the fourth season. (Possibly edging on Tier 4 in places...? The Winchesters are on a first name basis with Death, among others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:27:54-08:00","id":800799,"title":"","content":"I fully endorse the notion of divorcing Compacts and Conspiracies from Tier. As for the Compact vs. Conspiracy divide: while I understand The Kings Raven's desire to distinguish between them based on how large and organized the group is, that's a distinction without a (mechanical) difference. OTOH, a distinction between whether or not the org provides Endowments (or, if C&amp;C's \u201cCompact Endowments\u201d make it into 2e, whether the Endowments provided are temporal benefits or supernatural capabilities) is one that has mechanical importance; so if the distinction between Compact and Conspiracy is to be kept, I'd much rather it be based on the org's Endowments. <br /> <br /> On the subject of \u201cCompact Endowments\u201d: I like the idea of Compacts providing access to temporal benefits in the form of Compact-specific Merits; but I <i>don't</i> like calling them Endowments, as that unnecessarily confuses matters. If 2e adopts what C&amp;C calls Compact Endowments, I'd like to see them renamed: maybe call them Edges, or Benefits. <br /> <br /> As for the exclusivity of Endowments, I would say that <i>as a rule</i>, if you want your Hunter to have Endowments, have him join a Conspiracy. This rule would not be without exceptions, though: <b>Reliquary</b> predates <b>Hunter</b> and provides to individual characters what AKD provides as a Conspiracy; the Lucifuge don't provide their members with an Endowment; they gather those who already have the Endowment and provide them with accountability. The Loyalists of Thule arguably have the resources to provide their members with an Endowment in the form of access to Thaumaturgy or its equivalent; what puts them on the Compact side of things isn't that they <i>can't</i>; it's that they <i>don't</i>: if you join the Loyalists of Thule in order to pick up occult power, you've missed the point of the org. <br /> <br /> The thing is, these should remain <i>exceptions</i>; accessing supernatural powers without going through a Conspiracy to get them should be <i>hazardous</i> in a <b>Hunter</b> Chronicle, attracting unwanted attention and/or messing with the hunter's head (or possibly even shoving the hunter over into Slasher/Horror status); and for some Endowments, it may be flat-out impossible, with acquisition of the Endowment making you a de facto member of the Conspiracy (I'm thinking of the Conspiracies from <b>Spirit Slayers</b> and <b>Night Stalkers</b> in particular). I'm not sure I'd dedicate more than a box to Endowments outside the Conspiracies; but I <i>would</i> suggest doing at least that much. <br /> <br /> And finally, I'd be OK with the occasional Endowment being shared by a few Conspiracies \u2014 Advanced Armory, in particular, is something that I could see being provided outside the borders of the United States by rough analogues of Task Force Valkyrie (sometimes <i>very</i> rough analogues), or possibly even by an arms-dealing corporation with an interest in curtailing supernatural activities. But, like Endowments outside of Conspiracies, these should be exceptions to the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T10:34:56-08:00","id":801492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=800799#post800799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully endorse the notion of divorcing Compacts and Conspiracies from Tier. As for the Compact vs. Conspiracy divide: while I understand The Kings Raven's desire to distinguish between them based on how large and organized the group is, that's a distinction without a (mechanical) difference.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's what I don't understand. Why is &quot;without a (mechanical) difference&quot; a point against my idea?<br /> <br /> It's a distinction with an enormous thematic difference. Compacts are bottom up which means if you join you get a network of people who you mostly agree with on the important. Conspiracies are top down, which means if you join you get a commander giving you orders.<br /> <br /> That might not be a mechanical difference but it's an enormous difference to charachter and themes, which are arguably more important than mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=800799#post800799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> OTOH, a distinction between whether or not the org provides Endowments (or, if C&amp;C's \u201cCompact Endowments\u201d make it into 2e, whether the Endowments provided are temporal benefits or supernatural capabilities) is one that has mechanical importance; so if the distinction between Compact and Conspiracy is to be kept, I'd much rather it be based on the org's Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div> Meanwhile this feels superflacious to me. We already have a clear distinction between groups with powers or not. Scroll to the Endowment section and see if they're listed there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/797132-is-it-time-to-divorce-tier-from-cell-compact-conspiracy?p=800799#post800799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loyalists of Thule arguably have the resources to provide their members with an Endowment in the form of access to Thaumaturgy or its equivalent; what puts them on the Compact side of things isn't that they <i>can't</i>; it's that they <i>don't</i>: if you join the Loyalists of Thule in order to pick up occult power, you've missed the point of the org.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think the difference here is that the Loyalists of Thule (I'd say the same about the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood) can give members a tutuor. And a tiny minority of people will come out five years later knowing Thamaturgy with the rest flunking out. Meanwhile the Malleus Malleficrum can take some random construction worker and give him a tutor, and two weeks later he's got a Dot in Benediction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}